"""## STEP 4 — v6 patch and experiment queue

Edit settings at the top of the patch block (speed) or the queue block (weights, seeds, phases).
"""

# ═════════ STEP 4 — Install the v6 runtime patch and build the v6 experiment queue  (≈10 s–2 min) ═════════
# Settings you may edit are at the top of each block (patch settings, then queue settings below).
# Nothing already trained is retrained: runs with identical settings are found and reused.
# Runtime patch v6 = v5 speed patch + reviewer fixes. Runtime only; module files untouched.
# v6 additions (new options only; existing runs keep their identity and resume unchanged):
#   A. Optional temporal-change ("motion") loss: loss_kind "l1_ssim_motion@<w>" adds w × L1 error on
#      pixels that change between the last input frame and the target (the pixels a copy-last-frame
#      model gets wrong). "l1_ssim" is bit-for-bit the v5 objective.
#   B. Collapse detector + sanity gate, logged every epoch from the validation forecasts:
#      skill = 1 − MSE_model / MSE_persistence at t+1 and t+horizon, and
#      change ratio = mean|pred − last input| / mean|target − last input| (≈0 ⇒ copies the last frame).
#   C. Learning rate is a run option (default 2e-4 = all existing runs).
# Speed features carried over from v5:
#   1. Per-model microbatches (baselines were 1)            -> main speed-up, uses free GPU RAM
#   2. Vectorised per-sample loss (no Python loop per video) -> same objective, fewer kernel launches
#   3. Background batch prefetch + pinned memory            -> GPU never waits for data
#   4. Background Drive upload of checkpoints               -> training continues while Drive copies
#   5. cuDNN autotuner (benchmark=True)                      -> faster convolutions, not bitwise deterministic
#   6. Batched validation and batched held-out evaluation    -> same per-video metrics, far fewer calls
#   7. Software/source change no longer blocks resume        -> change is recorded, not hidden
# Effective batch (32), learning rate, epochs, loss, windows, splits and seeds are unchanged.
